  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 217 PM MDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThe 594 to 595 dam 500 mb high over NM and AZ Tuesday looks to \nreintensify to 598 to 599 dam and expand northwest to the Great \nBasin by Thursday before pivoting back to over the Four Corners and \nweakening to around 596-598 dam this weekend. High temperatures will \nnot be as hot as today, but still hotter than average for early \nAugust with mid 90s to low 100s common across lower elevations. \nDiurnal shower and thunderstorm chances will favor the higher \nterrain and nearby lower elevations along with the northeast and \neast central plains through Friday before shifting to mainly western \nand central NM this weekend.",
